 ## Unreleased
 
 ### Fixed
+- **Post-merge cleanup tolerates an already removed worker worktree** (`app/merge_operations.py`; V-1072). If worker removal races repository inspection or cleanup, a missing-file error is treated as a normal skip only after a separate filesystem check confirms the worktree root is gone. Existing-directory, permission and unverified failures still report errors; hub release failures remain visible. Merge results and all recoverability, input-provenance and deletion guards are unchanged. Python change follows the normal service lifecycle.
 - **Existing workers in source-only repositories can load and send without project memory** (`app/prompting.py`; V-1069). Optional memory lookup recognizes a missing or reports-only `.orchestra` in both a linked worktree and its base, so cold hydration no longer fails before the delivery path can submit. It removes stale prompt memory without initializing project state or changing worker bindings, branches or reports. Legacy state, migration markers, managed memory and unknown entries still require layout repair; authoritative layout guards remain strict. Python change follows the normal service lifecycle.
 - **Expected Codex quota refusals no longer trigger recurring-error alerts** (`app/error_watch.py`; V-1068). The Russian exhaustion message emitted by sessions is classified as quota/rate noise before and after numeric normalization, including unknown reset times. The same narrow matcher excludes these expected events from post-fix recurrence after normal fix registration. Matching is limited to the complete refusal and its reset fields; distinct provider, accounting, parser and availability failures remain actionable. English classification and recurrence policy for other noise are unchanged. Python change follows the normal service lifecycle.
 - **Full hub messages survive the message-field limit** (`app/backend_hub.py`, `app/hub_workspace.py`, `app/multicode_client.py`; V-1066). Fully composed inputs above 120,000 UTF-16 units travel intact through the existing private workspace transport with a short read-file message. First turns, resumed threads, replacement-thread fallback, steers and no-work retries use the same guarded route. Broker input files are atomic, checksum-verified, bounded by the existing workspace file limit and excluded from source uploads and result imports. Invalid parameters preserve the current thread; failed replacement launches retain its identity, and pending steers are acknowledged only after a confirmed start. No attachment truncation or additional provider call. Python change requires the normal idle-watcher lifecycle.
